Prefer the SDL controller bus over the macOS IOHID and XBOX360 buses.

winebus starts every available bus at IRP_MN_START_DEVICE.  On Linux a
successful SDL init sets options.disable_input so the udev bus skips the
same devices, but the macOS buses never consult that flag: bus_iohid.c and
bus_xbox360.c re-enumerate whatever SDL already reported.

That also leaves non-Xbox pads without XInput.  bus_iohid.c only sets
desc.is_gamepad for is_xbox_gamepad() vid/pids, so a DualShock 4 never gets
the WINEBUS\WINE_COMP_XINPUT compatible id, winexinput.sys never attaches,
and XInput-only titles see no controller at all.  The SDL bus classifies and
remaps controllers from its own mapping database, which covers Xbox and
PlayStation pads alike.

Start the macOS buses only when SDL is unavailable.  Both stop entry points
already return early on a NULL run_loop, so the unconditional stop calls in
IRP_MN_REMOVE_DEVICE stay correct for a bus that never started.

--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
@@ -1297,18 +1297,30 @@
         irp->IoStatus.Status = handle_IRP_MN_QUERY_DEVICE_RELATIONS(irp);
         break;
     case IRP_MN_START_DEVICE:
+    {
+        BOOL sdl_bus_started;
+
         bus_options_init();
 
         mouse_device_create();
         keyboard_device_create();
 
-        if (!sdl_driver_init()) options.disable_input = TRUE;
+        sdl_bus_started = !sdl_driver_init();
+        if (sdl_bus_started) options.disable_input = TRUE;
         udev_driver_init();
-        iohid_driver_init();
-        xbox_driver_init();
+        /* The SDL bus reports controllers as gamepads and remaps them onto the
+         * Xbox layout; the macOS IOHID and XBOX360 buses cannot do either, and
+         * would enumerate the same device a second time as a plain HID
+         * joystick.  Keep them as the fallback for when SDL is unavailable. */
+        if (!sdl_bus_started)
+        {
+            iohid_driver_init();
+            xbox_driver_init();
+        }
 
         irp->IoStatus.Status = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         break;
+    }
     case IRP_MN_SURPRISE_REMOVAL:
         irp->IoStatus.Status = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         break;
